<title>UK: DHL to create 500 new jobs in UK - paper.</title>
<headline>DHL to create 500 new jobs in UK - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight company DHL Worldwide Express plans to create 500 new jobs in the UK because of increased demand, The Times newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The company, which already employs 3,000 staff in the UK, said the new jobs will be in sales, customer services and couriers and will be spread throughout the country, the paper reported.</p>
<p>The new jobs will mean DHL has increased staff in the UK by almost a third in the past two years. Revenue from British companies rose by 24 percent last year, the paper said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6762</p>
</text>
